WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Human body cells carry 46 chromosomes.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.450
Gain just one extra chromosome, 47 in all,

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.480
and every cell of the
body carries the change.

4
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.460
Yet many plants live well with a
whole extra set of chromosomes.

5
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:15.810
Many crops do.

6
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:21.210
So how can a whole doubled set be
fine, when one extra chromosome is not?

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.890
In this mission, you'll watch one pair of
chromosomes fail to separate as gametes

8
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:26.840
are made.

9
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:32.000
Then you'll set one extra chromosome
side by side with a whole extra set.

10
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:37.190
Your mission: explain how some plants
thrive with doubled chromosome sets when

11
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.280
one extra chromosome
can change a whole body.
